story rb_top|Bell clapper|Bolt|The bell tower's iron clapper, taken down so the bell could not ring.
story rb_deep|Arcade till key|Bolt|The till key of the old shopping arcade, pulled out of its drawer by the pedlars before the arcade went under.
story rb_fixed|Crier's box working|Bolt|The crier's box, working again.
story rb_strong|Crier's strongbox open|Bolt|The crier's strongbox, opened with the market's own stall numbers.
note rb_hint Market crier's notice | MARKET CRIER'S NOTICE - in my own hand, since I'm not allowed to shout it.\n\nThe crier's box has been quiet since the arcade sank, and a market without a crier is just people standing near fish.\n\nMy bell's clapper is up in the pedlars' bell tower on Tin Peak. The Authority made me take it down after I rang the bell the night of the fire, and I hid it up there out of spite. The trail starts on the side toward the stalls. The box's till key the pedlars pulled out of the arcade before it went under - they keep it in their cave on the east shore, with everything else they won't sell.\n\nBring me both, and Raft Row will hear itself again.\n\n- Oswin, crier (retired, by order)
note rb_topchest Pedlars' bell tower deck box | A box lashed to the deck rail at the top of the pedlars' bell tower.
loot rb_topchest story:rb_top*1;Bolt*2;Scrap*2
note rb_deepchest Sunk arcade strongbox | A strongbox in the back room of the sunk arcade.
loot rb_deepchest Plastic*3;Nail*4;TradeToken*2
note rb_rewnote Crier's ledger | The crier's box hums, and the bell rings out over the stalls for the first time in a year. Somebody on the market cheers; somebody else drops a crate of eggs.\n\nInside the box: Oswin's ledger. Which stalls paid the Authority's levy to stay open, and which ones were burned. The levy was collected by a different clerk every week - but every page is signed off at the bottom in the same small, square hand: For the weight. A.C.\n\nOswin has written under the last one: What weight? Weight of what?\n\nOn the last page, the crier's round, the order he called the rows every morning: ROW C, ROW A, ROW D, ROW B. His strongbox opens the same way.
note rb_rewchest Crier's box reward | What the crier's box kept.
loot rb_rewchest TradeToken*3;Watermelon*2;Rope*2
note rb_ledge Climber's cache | A climber's cache on a ledge off the trail - rope, a flask, a few bolts.
loot rb_ledge Rope*2;Bolt*2;Scrap*2
prop rb_ledge loot.refill=0
loot rb_boatcrate Plastic*3;Scrap*2;MetalIngot*1
note rb_rowA Row A sign | MARKET ROW A\nStall 5 - tin and wire
note rb_rowB Row B sign | MARKET ROW B\nStall 3 - bells and pans
note rb_rowC Row C sign | MARKET ROW C\nStall 8 - shoes and rope
note rb_rowD Row D sign | MARKET ROW D\nStall 2 - fish and salt
note rb_strongchest Crier's strongbox | The crier's strongbox: the stall fees nobody ever paid back.
loot rb_strongchest TradeToken*4;CopperIngot*2;Rope*2

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Raft Row Bazaar
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Highwater's black market, lashed between four drowned towers: stalls, string lights, a garden key with hens, goats and fruit - and a back room the Authority doesn't know about. The second island of The City That Never Sank.
island on.arrive=message||Music, smoke, a hundred voices. A market floats between the roofs of four drowned towers, and nobody here asks to see a permit.

story backkey|Back room key|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|The merchant's back room key, from the drawer of his stall.

prop concrete tint.color=#9a9a94
prop concrete tint.amount=0.35
prop hens creature.count=3
prop goats creature.count=2
prop backroom if.open=has|story:backkey|1
prop backroom else.open=message||Locked. The merchant keeps the key on him - or in his stall's drawer.

note pricesign Bazaar price board | RAFT ROW - TODAY'S PRICES\n\nNails - cheap\nRope - cheap\nScrap - cheaper\nFilters - ASK\nClean water - ASK\n\nNo permits. No questions. No credit.
note shortage Shortage list | Chalked on a slate, rubbed out and written again many times -\n\nSHORT: filters, filter cloth, charcoal.\nSHORT: clean water.\nSHORT: anything the Authority stamps.\nSHORT: patience (mine).\n\nTwenty years I've had this stall and I've never seen a shortage go on this long. The prices go up, then the boats from Pumpcrown come in light, then the prices go up again. Funny, how the filters are always short, and the merchant on the north-east roof always has a new coat.\n\nAsk at the Free Fleet's stall. They find things.\n\n- Marta, corner stall
note teoschalk Free Fleet stall | FREE FLEET - WE FIND THINGS\n\nEngines, wheels, anything that floats. Ask for Teo.\n\nTeo is out. Teo is always out. Teo is at sea, where the Authority can't count him.\n\nTake what you need from the crate - the Fleet trusts you or it doesn't, and if it doesn't, you'll find out. If you're new: the wheel plans in there are good. My father drew them. He sailed out past Pumpcrown when the rules said nobody could, and he came back, which is more than the rules ever did.\n\n- T. Varga
note ledger Withheld stock ledger | The merchant's real book, in his small, careful hand.\n\nFilters received from the Authority: 400.\nFilters sold at the board: 0.\nFilters held back to raise the price: 400.\n\nThe Authority's cut, paid each week at Pumpcrown - to a clerk with a Council seal, never the same clerk twice.\n\nAt the bottom of the page, in a shakier hand: I didn't want this. They told me the market stays open as long as the board says ASK. My daughter drinks clean water. Other people's daughters don't. I write it down here so that somebody knows I know.\n\nSo the shortage is made. Someone should know.
note drawer Merchant's drawer | The stall's drawer: string, a broken pencil, a key on a tag that says BACK.
note enginecrate Engine stall crate | The engine stall's crate: the motor wheel's plans, bolts, a greasy rag.
note fleetstall Free Fleet stall | The Fleet's crate: the steering wheel's plans, and a chalked note - for the one who reads the board.
note backroom Back room | The back room's strongbox. Filters, stacked to the ceiling - and the merchant's warning.
note seedbox Garden box | The garden's seed box: beets and potatoes to plant.
loot enginecrate Blueprint_MotorWheel*1;Bolt*3;Nail*10
prop enginecrate loot.refill=0
loot fleetstall Blueprint_SteeringWheel*1;Rope*2;Plank*4
prop fleetstall loot.refill=0
loot drawer story:backkey*1;Rope*1
prop drawer loot.refill=0
loot backroom TradeToken*4;Plastic*4;Glass*2;story:raft-Vasagatan_BoltCutter*1
prop backroom loot.refill=0
loot seedbox Raw_Beet*4;Raw_Potato*2
prop seedbox loot.refill=0
place Note_Paper warning at 12 59 h=1.1 drop
prop warning obj.name=warning
prop warning beh.hidden=1
prop backroom on.open=show|warning\nmessage||Filters, stacked to the ceiling. On the strongbox, a folded note.
note warning Merchant's warning | Left on the strongbox, for whoever opened it -\n\nYou found the filters. Put them back and walk away.\n\nThe Authority takes its cut and leaves us alone. Tell the Fleet and they'll come with boats. Tell the Authority and they'll come with matches - ask the west stalls how that went.\n\nI am not a brave man. I sell things. I would like to go on selling things, in a market that is still here next week.\n\nEither way the market burns. Think about it. And if you have to go, go - but don't tell them where you got it.

prop marketzone zone.id=market
prop marketzone zone.radius=7
prop marketzone zone.message=Raft Row. Stalls under wooden roofs, string lights, flags - and prices nobody stamped.
prop fleetzone zone.id=fleet_stall
prop fleetzone zone.radius=3
prop fleetzone zone.message=The Free Fleet's stall. A flag with a gull on it, and nobody at the table.

note wardenreport Fire warden's report | FIRE WARDEN'S REPORT - Raft Row, west stalls\n\nCause: a lamp knocked over. Or so the Authority's clerk wrote, before he looked.\n\nSix stalls burnt. All six had refused to pay the Authority's 'market levy'. All six lamps were knocked over on the same night, in a flat calm, at the same hour. Fourteen years a fire warden, and I have never seen lamps so clumsy.\n\nNobody died. The pedlars dragged their stock out through the smoke and moved east to their caravans. They keep it in a cave now, where a lamp can't find it. The crier rang his bell all through the fire, and the Authority has not forgiven him.\n\nMy bolt cutters are in my tool box here. The pedlars chained up a chest by the old van to the south - use them, if you're one of us.\n\n- J. Okafor, fire warden
note pedlarcavechest Pedlars' stock | The pedlars' stock: the things a city on rafts runs out of first - and the drowned arcade's till key on a loop of wire.
loot pedlarcavechest story:rb_deep*1;Battery*1;Bolt*3;Rope*2;TradeToken*2
note rb_broadcast Councillor's broadcast | From the market's speaker, the same calm voice as the loop on five hundred -\n\n'Citizens of Raft Row. This is Councillor Crane. I know what is said about me in this market. I know the price of a filter here, and I know who sets it. I am not a fool, and I am not your enemy.\n\nThe Authority does not ration water out of spite. We ration it because this city cannot carry one more pound of anything. If you hoard, it sinks. If you riot, it sinks. If you sail off with the Fleet and leave your floors empty, the weight shifts, and it sinks.\n\nI ask you for patience. I have asked for nine years. I will ask again tomorrow.'\n\nScratched into the speaker's casing, deep: TURN IT OFF, ALDOUS.
note dobbs230 Complaint No. 230 | To the Harbor Council, Water Committee.\nCOMPLAINT No. 230\n\nSirs,\nToday I bought a filter at Raft Row for eleven trade tokens. It was one of mine. I know it was one of mine because I scratch a little W into every filter cloth before it leaves Pumpcrown, in case of exactly this.\n\nSo: my works makes a filter. The Authority takes the filter. The filter goes missing between Pumpcrown and the ration office. The filter comes back to me across a market stall at eleven tokens, and the stallholder calls me grandad.\n\nI am fifty-three.\n\nI would like the eleven tokens back, and an explanation, in that order.\n\nYours, still in hope, but less of it,\nWilmer Dobbs, Foreman, Pumpcrown Works\n\n(Pinned under the price board. Someone has added: ASK.)
note rb_tramtag Pedlar's tag | A brown card on a string, tied to a tin tram at the bottom of the crate - blue paint, a clockwork key, 6:40 on its side.\n\nNOT FOR SALE.\n\nA little girl from the Rookery swapped this for a bottle of clean water for her gran. She cried, and I cried, and her gran drank the water, so I suppose it was a fair trade. I said I'd hold it for her till she can buy it back. She told me her dad drove the real six-forty down Lowstreet before the street went under - blue door, number fourteen - and that he'll come back for it himself.\n\nI don't think he will. I'm holding it anyway. Hands off.\n\n- Rook, pedlar
note rb_friendnote A friend's note | Under the strongbox, the same folded paper, the same hurry -\n\nYou read the merchant's book. Four hundred filters held back, and the cut paid at Pumpcrown every week. Now you know the shortage is made, and you are starting to know who makes it.\n\nThe Free Fleet should hear this. They are the only people in Highwater with boats and no master. Their moorings are at Fleetbreak - band seven hundred. Ask for Teo Varga. He is loud, and proud, and mostly honest, which in this city is a lot.\n\nDon't trust the Councillor's voice. It is a very good voice. That is the trouble with it.\n\n- a friend
prop pedlarcavechest loot.refill=0
note pedlarcrate Pedlar's caravan | The caravan's stock crate: bottles of clean water at twice the Authority's price - and a list of who can't pay.
loot pedlarcrate Plastic*3;Glass*2;Leather*2
quest title=Prices Without Rules
quest intro=The tip said the bazaar sells what the Authority says doesn't exist. Find the market.
step reach|market|1|Walk onto the market between the towers
step read|Bazaar price board|1|Read the price board
step blueprint|Blueprint_MotorWheel|1|Take the motor wheel's plans from the engine stall's crate
step read|Shortage list|1|Read the shortage list at the corner stall
step reach|fleet_stall|1|Find the Free Fleet's stall on the east roof
step blueprint|Blueprint_SteeringWheel|1|Take the steering wheel's plans from the Fleet's crate
step read|Complaint No. 230|1|Read the complaint pinned under the price board
step read|Councillor's broadcast|1|Listen to the market's speaker
step open|Back room|1|Find the merchant's key and open the back room's strongbox
step read|Withheld stock ledger|1|Read the ledger in the back room
step catch|Chicken|1|Catch a hen from the garden for the Fleet's coop
step read|Fire warden's report|1|Read the fire warden's report in the burnt stall row, west of the key
step read|Market crier's notice|1|Read the market crier's notice by his silent box, north of the burnt row
step reach|rubbish_hill|1|Climb Rubbish Hill south of the market
step open|Pedlar's caravan|1|Open the stock crate at the pedlars' caravans on the east shore
step read|Pedlar's tag|1|Read the tag on what the pedlar won't sell
step collect|story:rb_deep|1|Find the pedlars' cave and take the arcade till key from their stock
step reach|rb_trail|1|Find the foot of the trail up Tin Peak, in the north-west
step reach|rb_summit|1|Climb the trail to the top of Tin Peak
step collect|story:rb_top|1|Climb the pedlars' bell tower and take the bell clapper from its deck
step read|Crier's ledger|1|Bring both to the crier's box and read what it shows
step collect|story:rb_strong|1|Find the four market row signs and open the crier's strongbox with their stall numbers
step read|Merchant's warning|1|Read the merchant's warning
step read|A friend's note|1|Read the folded note under the crier's strongbox
quest done=The shortage is made. The Free Fleet will want to know - their moorings are at Fleetbreak, band 700.
quest reward=Raw_Beet*3;Egg*2

